Action Vault&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
5/28/2002 7:25:14 AM<P>
Action Vault has completed their review of Star Trek: Bridge Commander. Here is a bit of what they thought:<p>
"Bridge Commander's annoyances are few, and most are slight. The primary exception is the difficulty in selecting stations on the bridge, which is a definite detriment to the enjoyment of the game. On the other hand, a gripping adventure, some intriguing gameplay and some notable visuals make Bridge Commander a fine addition to anyone's game library."<br>
<hr>
<a target="_new" href="
http://www.gamesxtreme.net/features.php?id=426">Star Trek: Bridge Commander Review</a><br>
GamesXtreme&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
3/18/2002 7:24:04 AM<P>
GamesXtreme has posted their review of the new Star Trek title for the PC. Here is a little of what they thought:<p>
"Any red-blooded Trekker worth his or her weight in dilithium has yearned for the chance to sit in the center seat, the ability to be the master of a 
mighty starship plying the spaceways. With the release of Star Trek: Bridge 
Commander these loyal fans will finally get their chance."<br>
